  "body": "Found while building the hole-work catalog case for #2862. Related catalog: #2392.\n\n## What happens\n\nA Circular operation with several radial passes generates blocking warnings. Verification refuses the program.\n\nReproduce on upstream/main 0510ff382 with the hole-work script from the #2862 branch. Change the Circular radius from 5 to 10 mm. Change its model envelope radius from 5.2 to 10.2 mm. Regenerate the mesh and run the script.\n\nParameters: center [30,30], tool EM-0600-4FL with 25 mm flutes, stepover 2, stepdown 2, top Z20, bottom Z0, clearance Z30, stock_to_leave 0. The stock is 90 x 90 x 20 mm. Entry is plunge.\n\nGeneration reports these warnings:\n\n- rapid move 69 travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)\n- rapid move 119 travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)\n\nHelix entry with helix_radius 1 also reports feed crossings at shared depth. Verification holds Circular in both cases. No program passes the post.\n\n## Expected\n\nCircular must generate safe links between its radial passes, or refuse the parameters before generation with a named cause.\n\n## Workaround\n\nA 5 mm radius with the same tool and plunge entry generates without warnings. The catalog uses this size.\n\nDone means: Pin the multi-pass case. Its links clear stock, verification passes, and the post stays blocked for a deliberately unsafe link.\n\nEffort: high. The fix changes motion links or verification under the safety floor.\n",
